{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/508779-abjurations-bindings-wards-and-all-that-twilight-stuff","id":508779,"title":"Abjurations, Bindings, Wards and all that Twilight stuff","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-08T23:36:48-07:00","id":508779,"title":"Abjurations, Bindings, Wards and all that Twilight stuff","content":"Hi. First, sorry if this has been discussed before (though to be fair I did make a search before posting). A simple question: Can a Demon be affected by Abjurations, Bindings, Wards, etc the way an Angel can? Normally I'd assume not since mechanically a Demon has kind of evolved beyond its original shape (and I don't assume werewolves, for instance, can be affected like spirits even though they are 'half-spirit&quot; and even use Essence). But the book doesn't address it either way, and actually it'd be fairly thematically appropriate in this case. I would say that the same techniques that can affect angels won't affect Demons and vice versa, though. A researcher has to &quot;reprogram&quot; the ritual to affect a heavily modified system, to put it into game parlance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T02:54:32-07:00","id":508850,"title":"","content":"Demons aren't ephemerals, and even if they were, demons don't have manifestations, bans or banes, or exist in twiight.<br /> <br /> No manifestations- no exorcism<br /> <br /> Don't exist in twilight- no abjuration<br /> <br /> Don't exist in twilight and don't have banes- no warding or binding<br /> <br /> So trying to ward a demon would be like trying to melt electricity. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T09:14:15-07:00","id":509039,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Fall isn't just disconnecting from the God-Machine, it warps you into a being of pure flesh, steel and blood. There's no way to do it because it's completely inapplicable once an angel becomes a Demon. Exiles...maybe, maybe not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T21:59:50-07:00","id":509575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/508779-abjurations-bindings-wards-and-all-that-twilight-stuff?p=508850#post508850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Demons aren't ephemerals, and even if they were, demons don't have manifestations, bans or banes, or exist in twiight.<br /> <br /> No manifestations- no exorcism<br /> <br /> Don't exist in twilight- no abjuration<br /> <br /> Don't exist in twilight and don't have banes- no warding or binding<br /> <br /> So trying to ward a demon would be like trying to melt electricity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. True. Although they do have &quot;Going Loud&quot;.<br /> <br /> 2. I'm reasonably certain being in or out of twilight doesn't impact the affect of an abjuration. I would certainly hate to think a Manifested spirit can't be abjured back to where it came from. Those poor humans!<br /> <br /> 3. Tch. Demons totally have Banes. They just call them glitches. If you want to ward up a house with salt to prevent the nasty thing that wants you dead from getting in, does it really matter whether you call that weakness a Bane or a Tell Glitch? Same basic idea. Why not use the same basic rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T22:29:30-07:00","id":509587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/508779-abjurations-bindings-wards-and-all-that-twilight-stuff?p=509575#post509575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. True. Although they do have &quot;Going Loud&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow I feel that brute-forcing a fundamental connection to the universe for an hour doesn't have the same resonance as definitionally being a process of the mechanistic <i>telos</i> that drives society for your entire active run.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. I'm reasonably certain being in or out of twilight doesn't impact the affect of an abjuration. I would certainly hate to think a Manifested spirit can't be abjured back to where it came from. </div> </div> </div>Abjurations specifically yank the Conditions supporting a manifestation out from under the creature in question. Demons are <i>the fleshy burned-in afterimage of an angel</i> and abjurations and the related systems apply to <i>ephemeral beings</i>, which by definition operate in the state of Twilight in the material world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Tch. Demons totally have Banes. They just call them glitches. </div> </div> </div>False equivalency that falls apart in the face of the demonic form lacking these qualities as innate traits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to ward up a house with salt to prevent the nasty thing that wants you dead from getting in, does it really matter whether you call that weakness a Bane or a Tell Glitch? </div> </div> </div>This is the same kind of stellar logic that has previously resulted in claims that the Centimani and the Pure are interchangeable. You're trying to apply a specific term for the weaknesses of flesh-lacking invisible monsters to flesh-having visible monsters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same basic idea. Why not use the same basic rules? </div> </div> </div>What Conditions are they being deprived of through abjuration or exorcism?<br /> <br /> Demonic existence is tautologically supported by demonic declaration of independent existence. They're plugged into <i>themselves</i>. You're not going to deprive them of that feed except by basic murder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T22:51:31-07:00","id":509597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/508779-abjurations-bindings-wards-and-all-that-twilight-stuff?p=509587#post509587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Conditions are they being deprived of through abjuration or exorcism?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the heart of it right here. Go back and reread the 2e rules for abjuration, binding and warding. Abjuration and exorcism dispel Influence Conditions. Wards and binding use the ephemera's bane. Demons don't have Influence Conditions or banes. There's nothing to remove by abjuring them, and nothing to make wards out of. Defecting to the human race means a more grounded, self-sufficient existence than that.<br /> <br /> Banes and glitches fill similar narrative roles, but banes are much more important to the relevant ephemera than glitches are to demons. Glitches seldom physically threaten the demon as much as an ephemeral bane does, and they often take forms that wouldn't give you anything to make the ward out of \u2014 if I've got a glitch that makes me stutter back and forth like time has come out of joint, that really sucks for my Cover's integrity, but it doesn't really give you anything to line a room with to keep me out. A lot of demons spend a considerable amount of their time without any glitches racked up, if they're careful about it, and having a glitch isn't meant to be as punishing as becoming vulnerable to being abjured by anybody with the mystical knowhow. After all, once they have that knowhow, they can spread it to others freely.<br /> <br /> The real reason, though, is that ephemeral beings are largely not meant to be player characters, so they're given rules that are good for players to interact with. Demons are meant to be player characters, and the corresponding rules aren't tuned to be turned against player characters in most cases. There's totally probably thaumaturgy or sorcerous rituals or whatever to protect against the influence of the Unchained somehow. But it's not going to be abjuration, it's going to be something that would be fun to throw at a player character and see them try to work around it, as much as it is for a player character to throw at an NPC demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T16:11:35-07:00","id":514598,"title":"","content":"Alternative: Make a Mystery Cult that provides Supernatural Merits that allows the use of this kind of activities to work on the Unchained, or even other Supernatural creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}